\f1\fs22 The Great Western Goat Track had been designed by someone who understood neither goats nor tracks, resulting in a road that seemed personally offended by the concept of straight lines. Tonight, it was about to be insulted further by a convoy of white Lincoln Continentals that looked like a funeral procession having a midlife crisis.\
"Brothers!" Major Memphis shouted into his CB radio, which was bedazzled with enough rhinestones to be visible from space. "Remember the plan! We hit fast, we hit hard, we hit with evolutionary superiority!"\
Twenty-three Lincolns roared up the mountain, their conditions ranging from "lovingly maintained" to "held together by sequins and prayer." Blue lights flashed from their roofs\'97some official, some clearly repurposed from disco balls. The sirens wailed Elvis's \'93Ground Hog" in B-flat.\
Chanta rode in the lead car, clutching the door handle as Specialist 5 Tulsa McLean took corners like personal insults. "Was the siren really necessary?"\
"Element of surprise, brother!" Tulsa shifted gears with violence. "No one expects a full Elvis assault at two in the morning!"\
"That's because it's insane!"\
"Exactly!"\
The first mansion appeared through the mountain mist like a monument to tax avoidance. Three stories of architectural arrogance squatted behind gates that probably cost more than most people's education.\
"Phase One!" Major Memphis barked. "Deploy the Sonic Disruption Squad!"\
Six Elvi piled out carrying Marshall stacks that had seen better decades. They began playing \'93Y\'92all Look Up" at volumes that violated several laws of physics. The mansion's security system, programmed to respond to conventional threats, had no protocol for weaponised rockabilly. Alarms stuttered, sensors failed, and somewhere in the house, a wine cellar's climate control system began weeping.\
"The Dawkins provides!" shouted Colonel Kalamazoo. "Their technology cannot withstand the power of evolutionary rhythm!"\
"Go, go, go!"\
Elvi swarmed over the gates like sequinned army ants. The B-team headed for the mansion's stasis units while the A-team maintained what they called "sonic cover" but was really just very loud chaos.\
Inside, Elvi 8,847 (known as "Suspicious Mick") found the kitchen. The stasis fridge stood there, humming with the confidence of appliances that don't know they're about to be liberated.\
"Sorry, brother," he told the fridge, then began the delicate work of extraction. The Gyges Disc sat in its housing like a pearl in an oyster that controlled time. He popped it free with a screwdriver blessed by the High Elvis himself.\
"Got one!" he shouted.\
"Check the wine cellar!" Major Memphis ordered. "Rich people always have wine cellars! It's evolution\'97they adapted to have more rooms to feel superior in!"\
Twenty minutes later, they'd stripped the mansion of five discs\'97one from the kitchen fridge, two from the wine cellar's climate control, one from the pool house, and one from what appeared to be a stasis unit dedicated entirely to keeping a single truffle fresh.\
"The decadence," muttered an Elvi, pocketing the truffle anyway.\
The convoy moved on, leaving behind a mansion whose appliances were slowly remembering how entropy worked.\
The second mansion fell even faster. The Elvi had refined their technique, which now included three-part harmonies that made security cameras weep static. The third mansion actually opened its own gates, its AI having achieved enlightenment through exposure to "Burning Love" in the key of chaos.\
By the fourth mansion, they'd developed a system:\
